From: Wren <wren@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] JSC: make the 32-bit (ARMv7) baseline JIT and DFG build again on 2.54

2.54 turned the JIT and the DFG off on every 32-bit build (see patch 0004, which turns them back on for ARMv7
Linux), and the 32-bit code paths stopped compiling. Fixes, each matching the 64-bit or the 2.50.5 code:

- Missing includes that 2.54 dropped from shared headers (JSCJSValue.h <wtf/Atomics.h>, InlineCacheCompiler.h
  CCallHelpers.h, ScriptExecutable.cpp CompilationResult.h).
- InlineCacheCompiler: 32-bit typos (propertyPayloadGPR -> propertyGPR), a link stub for
  getByIdMegamorphicGetterHandler, and ArrayLengthStore's hole fill for tag/payload values (64-bit unchanged).
- AssemblyHelpers: emitAllocateJSBigInt64 is 64-bit only; loadMegamorphicGetterSetter gets an unreachable 32-bit
  stub (LoadMegamorphicGetter is only created for JSVALUE64).
- MacroAssemblerARMv7: moveConditionally32 / moveConditionallyTest32 with an immediate thenCase (via
  addressTempRegister when the immediate is not a single instruction).
- DFG: the megamorphic and EnumeratorPutByVal nodes (64-bit backend only) fall back to the generic nodes on
  32-bit; MapStorage for 32-bit (empty JSValue for a null storage); string equality calls the operation instead
  of a 64-bit-only thunk; the 64-bit-only Array.prototype.sort nodes are guarded.

Reviewed before it was committed. The maintainer's JIT bring-up report (not in this repository) has the details.
---
